WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.260
- I heard though that you've always had

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.220
kind of sleep issues.

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.660
My son has -- he sleepwalks.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:04.500
You did you sleepwalk?

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.060
- I, you know what, I did.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:08.070
I had a little bit of sleepwalking.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:09.480
- Yeah, that's scary.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.030
- Well, and I hope it's
not like, hereditary

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.290
'cause my mom slept walked --

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.700
slept walked, sleepwalked?
- Sleep walked.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.750
- Slept walked.
- Dub, dub, dub.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.251
How do you?
- I don't really know.

00:00:17.251 --> 00:00:18.084
(audience coos)

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.170
- [Emma] Aw, there's my mom.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.918
We were both sleep
walkers, how about that?

00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:22.470
- There you go.
- I'll redirect that.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:23.940
- Yeah.
- We were both sleep walkers

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.130
and actually one time I was sleepwalking

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.770
and she was sleepwalking and
we actually ran into each other

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.080
and we were both so freaked out

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.120
and we realized we were both sleepwalking

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.250
and I was just like, this can't be good.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.360
Like, are the doors locked?

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.193
What's happening?

00:00:37.193 --> 00:00:38.550
- I know, it scares me
'cause I had a friend,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:39.383
and her brother had it,

00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.710
and he like walked out on the road

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:41.640
and he had no idea he was in the road.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:42.473
So I'm like terrified.
- No, that's --

00:00:42.473 --> 00:00:44.250
- And we have stairs in our house.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.300
- No!
- So I'm always like,

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.740
oh my god, don't find the stairs.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.420
- No, well I hope my
son's not a sleepwalker

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.480
but I mean he's two and we're
lucky he hasn't figured out

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.368
he can climb out of the crib
'cause he totally is capable.

00:00:53.368 --> 00:00:55.200
- Yeah.
- But he just hasn't,

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.033
which I thought was

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.577
very sweet of him.
- Yeah.

00:00:57.577 --> 00:01:00.060
That's different with boys and girls too.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.470
They're a little more behind.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.210
- Yeah, he's just, he's
happy to, you know,

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.650
just stay in the crib,
which is nice for now.

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:05.483
- Yeah.
- But I just know

00:01:05.483 --> 00:01:06.540
he's gonna climb out one day

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.248
and I just hope he doesn't
sleepwalk on top of that.

00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:10.248
- Enjoy baby jail while you have it.

00:01:10.248 --> 00:01:12.570
(Emma laughs)
Because once they get out

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.160
you are like, oh my god!
- No.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.750
- No, you can't draw on the walls.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.160
- No, now he know how to --
- For the fourth time.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.740
- open door knobs and
turn on and off lights.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:21.390
So, it's like there's a
ghost in my house sometimes.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:22.560
Like doors are open, lights are --

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:23.703
I'm like, what happened?
- Yeah.

00:01:23.703 --> 00:01:25.590
- I just turned all
this off and shut this.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.990
- We had a power outage like,
I don't know, months ago,

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:29.970
and my son was so terrified about it.

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:32.940
So now to say power, he like,
he goes around our house

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.020
and always turns off lights.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.077
- Love!
- He's the most --

00:01:35.077 --> 00:01:35.910
- Love that for him.
- Energy efficient 6-year old.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.650
- And for you!
- You've ever seen.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:38.820
He turns off every light.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.950
'cause he's afraid that the
power won't come back on.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:41.910
- Sad.
- I'm like,

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:43.290
I know there's gonna be some therapy there

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:44.123
in the future.
- That's cool.

00:01:44.123 --> 00:01:45.393
- It's fine, it's fine.

